    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n3\n001\n2\n11\n3\n010\n5\n11011",
        "output": "1\n0\n1\n5",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Consider the following sequence:\n\nChoose i=1i=1i=1. After this TTT becomes 010101 and KKK is equal to 111.\nAdd KKK to score\\text{score}score, to obtain score=1\\text{score} = 1score=1.\nChoose i=1i=1i=1. After this TTT becomes 111 and KKK is equal to 000.\nscore\\text{score}score remains 111.\n\nIt can be shown that no matter the sequence of operations, attaining score>1\\text{score}\\gt 1score>1 is not possible.\nTest case 222: As all the characters of SSS are the same, the maximum possible score after the algorithm will be 000.\nTest case 444: Consider the following sequence:\n\nChoose i=2i=2i=2. After this TTT becomes 101110111011 and KKK is equal to 222. Our score is 222.\nChoose i=4i=4i=4. After this TTT becomes 101101101 and KKK is equal to 222. Our score is 444.\nChoose i=3i=3i=3. After this TTT becomes 101010 and KKK is equal to 111. Our score is 555.\nChoose i=2i=2i=2. After this TTT becomes 111 and KKK is equal to 000. Our score is 555.\n\nIt can be shown that 555 is the maximum score we can reach."
      }
    ]
